WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
The David Pakman Show at David Pakman Dotcom.
We're now more than a week into Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.640
Biden's presidency, there are&nbsp;
certainly things to criticize.&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.760
For example, Joe Biden said two thousand dollar&nbsp;
checks are going out right away. If Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.480
win the two Georgia seats, they haven't. Now,&nbsp;
it's not clear exactly what will be in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.680
covid relief bill. It's not exactly clear when&nbsp;
that is going to be happening. So there's no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:27.120
question that there are criticisms here. But&nbsp;
if we take a sort of fair and comprehensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:33.760
approach to the question, how does Joe Biden's&nbsp;
first week compare to Donald Trump's four years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.520
I would make the case and I would feel confident&nbsp;
making it that Joe Biden has done more good in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.520
his first eight or nine days in office,&nbsp;
eight days in office, I guess it's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.880
than Donald Trump did in his entire four&nbsp;
years. A lot of this has to do with the virus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:56.480
the coronavirus task force being invigorated,&nbsp;
bringing in actual qualified doctors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.160
increasing vaccination. We're already up&nbsp;
to one point two million vaccines a day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:08.560
figuring out where are these discrepancies in&nbsp;
terms of vaccines, getting vaccines out to people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:14.720
number of vaccinating locations going up&nbsp;
dramatically, starting to be very clear about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:21.600
possible trajectory trajectory of the virus. That&nbsp;
alone is absolutely huge. But then you look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.720
pausing the arms sales to Saudi Arabia and the&nbsp;
United Arab Emirates, reversing a lot of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:34.000
bad decisions made by Donald Trump, including&nbsp;
Joe Biden, getting us back into Paris climate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:42.080
back into the O, reversing the trans military&nbsp;
ban, working to promote racial equality through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.720
executive orders after Donald Trump did whatever&nbsp;
he could to get rid of any executive orders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.920
that said, hey, we should really look at&nbsp;
this or we should really look at that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.800
starting to actually put together some potential&nbsp;
progress on immigration, which has been.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.640
So it's not just that the&nbsp;
discussion has been fraught,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:09.520
but it's been such a failure under the Trump&nbsp;
administration looking at environmental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.440
regulations that are put back in when they&nbsp;
were once Trump undid via executive order,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:22.720
but also canceling Keystone XL pipeline.
I mean, I could go on and on and on with the list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:31.040
but the amount that he has been able to do&nbsp;
in these first eight or so days really is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:36.960
more of a counterbalance to Donald Trump's&nbsp;
four years than I could have ever imagined.&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.960
And my promise to you when Joe Biden, even&nbsp;
before Joe Biden won and then when he won,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.640
and then when he was confirmed by the&nbsp;
Electoral College and when he was inaugurated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.040
is that we are going to keep Joe Biden&nbsp;
accountable to the promises that he made.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.200
But when Joe Biden does things that are good,&nbsp;
I'm going to tell you that he did good things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.520
It doesn't mean he's perfect. It doesn't mean the&nbsp;
Democratic Party is now a bastion and beacon of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.920
progressivism. It simply means that sometimes&nbsp;
presidents do things that are good and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:12.400
should be applauded for that. And I think what has&nbsp;
been most fascinating to see about this is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:19.920
the country seems to see it. Joe Biden's&nbsp;
first approval rating, 63 percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:26.560
higher than Donald Trump's approval rating at&nbsp;
any time during his presidency. Remember that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.800
Donald Trump never even hit 50 percent at any time&nbsp;
during his presidency and presidential approval.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:40.960
Joe Biden already at 63 percent, 69 percent&nbsp;
approval of Joe Biden's handling of coronavirus in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:48.000
these early days, 80 81 percent approval of Joe&nbsp;
Biden's federal mask mandate and and national&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:54.160
mask sort of request, I think is the right way to&nbsp;
call it. So we are in a very polarized situation.&nbsp;

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:00.240
Twenty five, twenty eight, 30 percent of the&nbsp;
country is off the deep end in terms of radical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.640
ignorant politics, as I call&nbsp;
it. So when you consider that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:11.840
these really are very, very good numbers for&nbsp;
Joe Biden and we are going to continue tracking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:17.520
his promises and what he does. But&nbsp;
the first seven, eight, nine days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.400
I am very pleased with and I'm even yesterday we&nbsp;
had a voicemail from a Bernie supporter who said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:27.120
I voted Bernie. But I have to tell you, I'm&nbsp;
pleasantly surprised by a lot of what's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:33.040
on. And I do believe that in terms of the most&nbsp;
pressing thing, what's happening with vaccinations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.280
is excellent. And I hope that we can soon be&nbsp;
at two, two and a half million vaccines a day.

